      "comment": "GRANDAD'S ADICTION (5) brings the most appealing recent profile after winning a NMW1Y at Belmont, where he was near the top of an open market and fought gamely. He gets weight relief, has been consistent this season and has enough 1800m grounding to justify top billing. LIEN HYPHEN (3) is the danger off stronger Saturday-company form, beaten just over two lengths in a 1 Metro Win on soft ground, and her record around 1800m is a key asset. SAFARI BOY (7) improved at Bunbury when fifth in a CL3 and is better placed with weight relief, though he still has to turn recent form into a sharper winning effort. HARD QUESTIONS (1) is flying after a Mingenew win and an Open second at Carnarvon, but the 1800m record keeps him more to the place line despite his strong current form. ODIN OMEN (6) is next best.",
